WEBVTT

00:00.400 --> 00:18.781
Keep shared policy in dot deslop dot toml, beside the scan root. That is the directory you ask Deslop to analyse. Use the config flag when your policy lives elsewhere. A missing configuration file uses built-in defaults, so commit your settings when the team needs consistent behavior.

00:19.631 --> 00:39.874
Choose exclusions carefully. Exclude removes a file before analysis. Report hide still analyses the file, but hides its occurrences. A cluster disappears only when all its members are hidden. This lets a match between handwritten and generated code remain visible, without showing every generated-only cluster.

00:40.724 --> 00:57.934
Use command-line flags for a single run. A flag overrides its matching configuration key. Fail over supplies a duplication ceiling; no fail over clears the ceiling for that run. These options control the gate, rather than fixing or removing duplicated code.

00:58.784 --> 01:17.746
A threshold makes excessive duplication fail the run with exit code three. The report remains available to inspect. Without a threshold, duplication alone does not fail the scan; runtime and usage errors still can. Review the report, agree on the policy, and keep that policy with your project.
